scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-c.a-dc-135-1999f-1.pdf-1,courts-coa-c.a-dc-135-1999f-1.pdf,,COA,1999,A party invoking the provisions of section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance to defeat the ownership of an adverse claimant to immovable property must establish a starting point for their acquisition of prescriptive rights.,"Where a party invokes the provisions of section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance in order to defeat the ownership of an adverse claimant to immovable property, the burden of proof rests squarely and fairly on him to establish a starting point for his acquisition of prescriptive rights.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
