scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_colombo_16_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_colombo_16_99.pdf,,COA,,"A defendant must establish that they have possessed the land in question for a period of 10 years immediately prior to the institution of the action, as contemplated in section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.","proof of undisturbed an uninterrupted possession by a defendant in any action, or by those under whom he claims, of immovable property, by a title adverse to or independent of that of the claimants or plaintiff in such action that is to say a possesswn unaccompanied by payment of rent of produce or performance of service or duty or by any other act by the possessor from which an acknowledgement of the right existing in another person would fairly and naturally be inferred for 10 years previous to the bringing of the action.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
