scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_1186_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_1186_98.pdf,,COA,,A plaintiff cannot claim prescriptive rights to land when they are not certain that it belongs to the defendant.,"Hence, it is clear that the appellant could not have claimed prescriptive rights to the disputed land when he was not certain that it belonged to the respondent when claiming possession adverse to his rights.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_123_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_123_99.pdf,,COA,,A party invoking the provisions of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance to defeat ownership must establish a starting point for their acquisition of prescriptive rights.,"lt is trite law that where a party to an action for a declaration of title to a land invokes the Provisions of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance in order to defeat the ownership of an adverse claimant to immovable property, the burden of proof rests squarely and fairly on him to establish a starting point for his or her acquisition of prescriptive rights.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_1292_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_1292_98.pdf,,COA,,A party claiming prescriptive title must satisfy the court that they have established the ingredients in Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.,In order to prescribe to the said lots 9 and 10 it is important for the party concerned to satisfy Court that he has established the ingredients in Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.,SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_gampaha_1133_00.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_gampaha_1133_00.pdf,,COA,,"An oral agreement affecting immovable property is not enforceable in law unless it is in writing and signed by the party making the same, or by some person lawfully authorized by him or her, in the presence of a licensed notary public and two or more witnesses present at the same time.","In terms of Section 2 of the Prevention of Fraud Ordinance no contract or agreement affecting land or other immovable property shall be of force or avail in law unless the same shall be in writing and signed by the party making the same, or by some person lawfully authorized by him or her in the presence of a licensed notary public and two or more witnesses present at the same time, and unless the execution of such writing, deed, or instrument be duly attested by such notary and witnesses.",SRC001-s2,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_homagama_1113_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_homagama_1113_98.pdf,,COA,,"A person can claim prescriptive title to land if they have been in possession of the land for a period of over ten years, adverse to the rights of the original owner.","In the circumstances, it is abundantly clear that the respondent had been in possession of the land claimed by the plaintiff for a period of well over ten years prior to the filing of this action on 03.05.1991, adverse to the rights of the plaintiff which is the criteria applicable to claim prescriptive title in terms of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_kegalle_842_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_kegalle_842_99.pdf,,COA,,A lessee who has entered into occupation is precluded from disputing his lessor's title until he has first restored the property in fulfilment of his contractual obligations.,Indeed a lessee who has entered into occupation is precluded from disputing his lessor's title until he has first restored the property in fulfilment of his contractual obligation.,SRC029-s116,none,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_kuliyapitiya_293_00.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_kuliyapitiya_293_00.pdf,,COA,,A claim for recovery of property belonging to a temple is not barred by prescription.,"In the case of any claim for the recovery of any property, movable or immovable, belonging or alleged to belong to any temple, or for the assertion of title to any such property, the claim shall not be held to be barred or prejudiced by any provision of the Prescription Ordinance:",SRC071-s34,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_mathugama_367_1998.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_mathugama_367_1998.pdf,,COA,1998,The burden of proof rests squarely and fairly on the defendant to establish a starting point for their acquisition of prescriptive rights.,"In a case of this nature once the Plaintiff-Respondent proves title by way of a transfer deed and seek to establish paper title, the burden is on the Defendant to establish superior title by prescriptive rights. i.e to satisfy the requirements of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_mt.lavinia_619_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_mt.lavinia_619_99.pdf,,COA,,A party cannot deny an admission they made in a lease agreement.,"The contention of the learned President's Counsel on this matter, in my opinion is not without merit.",SRC029-s21,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_mt.lavinia_926_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_mt.lavinia_926_99.pdf,,COA,,"A court must investigate the title of parties, especially when it comes to claims of prescription among co-owners, as required by law.",It has been pointed out over and over again that it is the solemn duty of the learned District Judge to investigate the title of the parties specially with regard to claim of prescription among eo-owners as required in terms of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.,SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
