scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-cala_dc_mt.lavinia_41_2007.pdf-1,courts-coa-cala_dc_mt.lavinia_41_2007.pdf,,COA,2007,A bank can proceed to auction a property mortgaged to it while a partition case is pending in respect of that property.,"In the absence of any statutory bar, Licensed Banks are entitled to proceed to auction a property mortgaged to a Bank while a partition case is pending in respect of that property.",SRC004-s66,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-HCC-21-20-JUDGMENT-4.pdf-1,courts-coa-HCC-21-20-JUDGMENT-4.pdf,,COA,,"A witness's credibility is not affected by trivial contradictions in their testimony, especially when they are consistent on the main points of the incident.","I hold that this trivial contradiction does not affect the credibility of this witness. On the other hand, he will remember what is important, which should have always been in his memory, because that incident would not fade from his memory.",SRC029-s165,none,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-RII-0061-24-EDITED-1.pdf-1,courts-coa-RII-0061-24-EDITED-1.pdf,,COA,,"A lessor is entitled to terminate a lease agreement prior to its expiry if the lessee breaches any of the terms, conditions, covenants, obligations, or duties set out in the agreement.","In terms of section 3(b) of the Act, a lessor is entitled to terminate the lease agreement prior to the expiry of the period of the lease agreement due to a breach by the lessee of any of the terms, conditions, covenants, obligations, or duties set out in the agreement.",SRC001-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-TAX-03-2020-Judgment.pdf-1,courts-coa-TAX-03-2020-Judgment.pdf,,COA,2020,The receipt of an appeal shall be acknowledged within thirty days of its receipt.,"Section 165(6) of the IRA 2006 provides that the receipt of an appeal shall be acknowledged within thirty days of its receipt. Where such acknowledgment is issued, the date appearing on the letter of acknowledgment is deemed to be the date of receipt of the appeal for the purposes of the section.",SRC001-s6,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
