scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-Writ-152-24.pdf-1,courts-coa-Writ-152-24.pdf,,COA,,"The power of review of the Board is limited to the orders dismissing an application, granting a certificate, approving a settlement, or before the payment of a compounded debt is completed.","Therefore, as the learned Counsel for the 1st respondent correctly contended, an order made only on those four instances could be reviewed in terms of Section 54 of the Ordinance.",SRC001-s1,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-WRT-0054-20.pdf-1,courts-coa-WRT-0054-20.pdf,,COA,,The jurisdiction of the Court under Article 140 is supervisory in nature and primarily concerned with the legality of administrative action rather than the adjudication of disputed private rights.,It is well settled that the jurisdiction of this Court under Article 140 is supervisory in nature and is primarily concerned with the legality of administrative action rather than the adjudication of disputed private rights.,SRC029-s83,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-WRT-497-23-JUDGMENT.pdf-1,courts-coa-WRT-497-23-JUDGMENT.pdf,,COA,,"A bank can aggregate multiple loan facilities to surpass the threshold of Rs. Five Million for the purpose of section 5A of the Recovery of Loans by Banks Act, if the principal amount borrowed due and owing to the bank on the loan granted exceeds Rs. Five million at the point of default.","For the purpose of section 5A, a Bank is not permitted to aggregate multiple loan facilities, all secured by the same mortgage, in order surpass the threshold of Rs. Five Million. The principal amount of each loan facility should exceed Rs. Five million.",SRC002-s5A,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
