scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_108_2022-1.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_108_2022-1.pdf,,SC,2022,A mere presence of a prayer for a declaration of title cannot make the action a rei vindicatio action.,Mere presence of a prayer for a declaration of title cannot make the action a re vidicatio action.,SRC029-s116,none,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_10_2013.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_10_2013.pdf,,SC,2013,Mere possession does not suffice to prove prescription; adverse possession must be established.,"If that be so it would become adverse from 06.02.2003 or 07.02.2003 by forcible erection of fence, on the western boundary to lot 21. Plaintiff instituted action on 02.06.2003 which is shortly after the above erection of the fence. Therefore the period of 10 years cannot be contemplated or computed in this background.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
