scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_117_2012.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_117_2012.pdf,,SC,2012,"Parole evidence is permitted to prove a constructive trust between parties, despite Section 2 of the Prevention of Frauds Ordinance and Section 92 of the Evidence Ordinance.","In order to prove a constructive trust, is parole evidence permitted in view of the principles set out in Section 2 of the Prevention of Fraud Ordinance and Section 92 of the Evidence Ordinance? This question was discussed in the case of Dayawathi and Others Vs Gunasekara and Another [1991] 1 SLR 115.",SRC001-s2,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
