scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_120_2014.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_120_2014.pdf,,SC,2014,A power of attorney granted by a minor is void if the transaction is not for the benefit of the minor.,"It appears that she had considered that the Plaintiff, as per his age, was a minor in terms of our law at the time the said Power of Attorney was given and when the transaction is not for the benefit of the minor, it is not valid against the minor, and as such the Power of Attorney and the transactions based on that Power of Attorney are void.",SRC071-s10,bad-source,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
