scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_balapitiya_830_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_balapitiya_830_98.pdf,,COA,,A party invoking the provisions of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance to defeat an adverse claimant's ownership of immovable property must establish a starting point for their prescriptive rights.,"Where a party invokes the provisions of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance in order to defeat the ownership of an adverse claimant to immovable property, the burden of proof rests squarely and fairly on him to establish a starting point for his or her acquisition of prescriptive rights.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_colombo_16_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_colombo_16_99.pdf,,COA,,"A defendant must establish that they have possessed the land in question for a period of 10 years immediately prior to the institution of the action, as contemplated in section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.","proof of undisturbed an uninterrupted possession by a defendant in any action, or by those under whom he claims, of immovable property, by a title adverse to or independent of that of the claimants or plaintiff in such action that is to say a possesswn unaccompanied by payment of rent of produce or performance of service or duty or by any other act by the possessor from which an acknowledgement of the right existing in another person would fairly and naturally be inferred for 10 years previous to the bringing of the action.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_colombo_780_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_colombo_780_98.pdf,,COA,,"A plaintiff can claim prescriptive title to land if they have been in uninterrupted possession of the land for ten years, without paying rent or performing any service or duty.",This position in law is supported by many authorities. Maasdorp's Institutes (7th Edition Vol2 at 96) Wigneswaran J in Leisa and another V Simon and Another [2002 (1) SLR 148] Pathirana V Jayasundera [58 NLR 169] Dona Cecilia V Cecilia Perera and others [1987 (1) SLR 235] Wijesundara and others v Constantine Dasa and another [1987 (2) SLR 66] I will now turn to consider whether the learned District Judge correctly evaluated the evidence and applied the law relevant thereto when he accepted the prescriptive rights .I 3 of the plaintiff rejecting the defence taken up by the defendant.,SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_1186_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_1186_98.pdf,,COA,,A plaintiff cannot claim prescriptive rights to land when they are not certain that it belongs to the defendant.,"Hence, it is clear that the appellant could not have claimed prescriptive rights to the disputed land when he was not certain that it belonged to the respondent when claiming possession adverse to his rights.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_123_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_galle_123_99.pdf,,COA,,A party invoking the provisions of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance to defeat ownership must establish a starting point for their acquisition of prescriptive rights.,"lt is trite law that where a party to an action for a declaration of title to a land invokes the Provisions of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance in order to defeat the ownership of an adverse claimant to immovable property, the burden of proof rests squarely and fairly on him to establish a starting point for his or her acquisition of prescriptive rights.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
