scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_35_2009.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_35_2009.pdf,,SC,2009,A cause of action based on a written promise or contract is not prescribed in law if the action is brought within six years from the date of the breach of such promise or contract.,"Before it could be said that the action falls under section 6 of the Ordinance, it must be shown that the action is based upon a written promise or contract.",SRC071-s6,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_3_2009.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_3_2009.pdf,,SC,2009,An action based on a written contract is not prescribed if brought within six years from the date of the breach of such contract.,"Section 6 of the Prescription Ordinance provides that; “No action shall be maintainable upon ... any written promise, contract, bargain, or agreement, ... unless such action shall be brought within six years from the date of the breach of such ... contract, bargain or agreement, ... from the date when such note or bill shall have become due, or of the last payment of interest thereon.”",SRC071-s6,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
